From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Load web fonts and shape text on the CoreText of iOS 6

No @font-face had ever loaded a font on this port, and every form control was
painted in a fully transparent colour. This loads web fonts, looking for the
WOFF2 library when the build asks for it, and draws form controls. Joined emoji
compose into one glyph because the character break iterator uses ICU; the
system font takes a weight; font feature tags are translated to the pairs this
CoreText understands; an empty glyph coverage is not read; blend filters take
the non-separable modes; and a missing localized string shows the English text.
